    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "splint, lath, esp. one of the plates or strips of overlapping metal of which certain portions of medieval armor were sometimes composed (esp. for protecting the elbows); also moderately flexible piece of wood used in manufacture (e.g. of hats) (OED s.v. splint) | a moderately flexible piece of wood used in manufacture (e.g. of hats) (OED s.v. splint) | splint, esp. one of the plates or strips of overlapping metal of which certain portions of medieval armor were sometimes composed (esp. for protecting the elbows) (OED s.v. splint) | one of the plates or strips of overlapping metal of which certain portions of medieval armor were sometimes composed (esp. for protecting the elbows) (OED s.v. splint) | one of the plates or strips of overlapping metal of which certain portions of medieval armor were sometimes composed (especially for protecting the elbows) (OED s.v. splint) | splint, lath, especially one of the plates or strips of overlapping metal of which certain portions of medieval armor were sometimes composed (especially for protecting the elbows); also moderately flexible piece of wood used in manufacture (e.g. of hats) (OED s.v. splint) | a moderately flexible piece of wood used in manufacture (e.g. of hats) (OED s.v. splint) | a moderately flexible piece of wood used in manufacture hats (OED s.v. splint) | a moderately flexible piece of wood used in manufacture of hats (OED s.v. splint) | a slender, moderately long and frequently flexible, rod or slip of wood cut or cleft off and serving for some particular purpose, especially as a lath or wattle, or prepared for use in some manufacture (OED s.v. splint n. 2a, cf. splinter n. 3a) | splint, lath, especially one of the plates or strips of overlapping metal of which certain portions of medieval armor were sometimes composed (esp. for protecting the elbows); also moderately flexible piece of wood used in manufacture (e.g. of hats) (OED s.v. splint) | one of the metal plates making up or reinforcing armor (MED s.v. splete n. (1)) | spleet a small strip of split wood or willow, used to make hats (OED s.v. spleet n.)" ;
